  <section class="essay about">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="dek">I’m tinylion1024. I write about the AI shifts that change product form, engineering practice, and business structure—not every passing launch.</p>
    <div class="essay-rule"></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The publication follows five threads: Models & Reasoning, Agent Products & UX, AI Software Engineering, AI Business & Growth, and AI & Society. The aim is to connect technical capability, user behavior, and commercial consequence in one argument.</p>
      <p>The editorial standard is equally deliberate: separate evidence from interpretation, link claims that can change, explain growth through product mechanics, and discuss engineering through workflows that readers can inspect and test.</p>
      <p>Chinese is the primary edition. Every essay also has an English counterpart rewritten for an international reader. The five threads connect into a maintained research archive rather than a publication calendar.</p>
      <p>If you build AI products, design agent workflows, or study how new technology reshapes organizations and markets, RSS is the most dependable way to follow along.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
